{title: Joktan's Son}
{subtitle: Genesis 10:26; 1 Chronicles 1:20}
{key: Eb}
{tempo: 74}
{time: 4/4}

{comment: Intro}
| [Eb] | [Eb] | [Ab/Eb] | [Eb] |
| [Ab/Eb] |

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[Eb]Joktan fathered Almodad
[Bb]Sheleph came next in the line
[Cm]Hazarmaveth and Jerah
In the [Ab]east they drew near
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[Eb]Sons of Shem after the [Bb]Flood
Descendants of Noah's blood
A [Cm]family tree from the start
In [Ab]the land of the east part
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[Eb]Thirteen sons in the list
Of [Bb]Joktan's lineage distinct
[Cm]In the mountain regions high
[Ab]Under the open sky
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 4}
[Eb]Genesis records their names
[Bb]Chronicles repeats the same
[Cm]From the beginning of days
[Ab]To the light of our eyes
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 5}
[Cm]Part of the nations spread
[Ab]After the Tower's head
[Eb]Scattered across the land
By the [Bb]Father's command
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Outro}
Sheleph remains in the text
{end_of_verse}

{comment: Outro (instrumental)}
| [Eb] | [Ab/Eb] | [Eb] | [Eb] |
